      "content": "but the \"electrical interaction\" thing sounds like a cover story. if a company wanted to exfiltrate data without being caught, wouldn't using sub-audible light pulses during high-bandwidth activity be a perfect way to do it? it's way more subtle than a bugged mic. if my house is basically a giant sensor for them because of my smart home setup, how can i even tell if i'm being monitored?",
